## Unknown stock classifier — resolution order

When any stock has `sector === "Unknown"` after JSON lookup, `enrichStockDetails()` runs:

```
1. lookupIndexStockFromDB(symbol)    ← DB cache (instant, no external API)
2. getTcbsStockMeta(symbol)          ← TCBS company API (authoritative real data)
   https://apipubaws.tcbs.com.vn/tcanalysis/v1/ticker/{symbol}/overview
   Returns: organName (VI), organNameEn (EN), icbName3, icbName4, exchange
3. callLlm(classify prompt)          ← LLM fallback only if TCBS misses
```

**Always prefer step 2 over step 3.** TCBS gives real data; LLM can hallucinate company identity (e.g. classifying HHV as "Real Estate" when it's "Infrastructure").

Result is always saved to `stock_symbol` DB. Future requests never leave step 1.

### If classifier returns wrong sector

1. Check `stock_symbol` DB row — delete or update it manually.
2. The next `getStock()` call will re-classify.
3. Check `normalizeSector()` in `src/lib/providers/tcbs.ts` — add the ICB label mapping if it's missing.

### If TCBS is unavailable

The classifier falls through to LLM. LLM classification is marked with `provider !== "tcbs"` (implicit — check if the saved name matches TCBS data after recovery). Set the correct sector manually in `stock_symbol` if LLM produced wrong data.

