## VN30/VN100 update — data flow

```
POST /api/admin/update-index
  → fetchTcbsIndex("VN30")    https://apipubaws.tcbs.com.vn/stock-insight/v1/index/VN30/components
  → fetchTcbsIndex("VN100")
  → [fallback] fetchSsiIndex  https://iboard-query.ssi.com.vn/v2/stock/watchlist?watchlistCode=VN30
  → upsertIndexMembers(vn30Set, vn100Set)
      prisma.stockSymbol.update/create  (is_vn30, is_vn100, updated_at)
      prisma.stockSymbol.updateMany     (clears stale flags for removed members)
  → clearMetaCache()           resets in-memory JSON-backed map
```

**VN30 rebalancing calendar:** HOSE reviews quarterly (Mar, Jun, Sep, Dec). Weekly Monday cron is enough — no same-day latency requirement.

### Extending to include name/sector during index update

Currently `update-index` only sets `is_vn30`/`is_vn100`. If you want to also populate name + sector for all VN30/VN100 members in one pass, extend `upsertIndexMembers` to call `fetchTcbsCompanyOverview(symbol)` per member and include `name`, `sector` in the upsert. This avoids the lazy-load cost when users first view those stocks.

