## Adding a new external data provider

Pattern used by `src/lib/providers/tcbs.ts`:

```ts
const HEADERS = { Accept: "application/json", "User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 ..." };

export async function fetchMyProvider(symbol: string): Promise<MyData | null> {
  try {
    const res = await fetch(`https://api.myprovider.com/v1/${symbol}`, {
      headers: HEADERS,
      next: { revalidate: 3600 },   // CDN cache; 0 for always-fresh
      signal: AbortSignal.timeout(5000),
    });
    if (!res.ok) return null;
    const raw = await res.json();
    if (!raw.someRequiredField) return null;
    return raw;
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
```

Rules:
- Always `AbortSignal.timeout(N)` — external APIs can hang.
- Always `return null` on failure — never throw from a provider; callers chain providers.
- Set `next: { revalidate: 0 }` only for data that must be real-time (index composition fetch). Use `3600` for company metadata that rarely changes.
- Add the provider to `src/lib/providers/` — one file per provider.

