## Neon HTTP — upsert safety for stock_symbol

`prisma.stockSymbol.upsert()` works because `stock_symbol` has a single-field PK; Prisma generates one `INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE` without a transaction wrapper. If you see `"Transactions are not supported in HTTP mode"`, replace with:

```ts
import { Prisma } from "@/generated/prisma/client";
await prisma.$executeRaw(
  Prisma.sql`INSERT INTO stock_symbol (symbol, name, sector, exchange, updated_at)
    VALUES (${sym}, ${name}, ${sector}, ${exchange}, NOW())
    ON CONFLICT (symbol) DO UPDATE SET
      name = EXCLUDED.name, sector = EXCLUDED.sector,
      exchange = EXCLUDED.exchange, updated_at = NOW()`,
);
```

Do NOT use `createMany + skipDuplicates` or multi-model transactions in any route that runs on Vercel (`DB_DRIVER=http`).

